{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/685812-scions-and-hunters","id":685812,"title":"Scions and Hunters","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-10-02T08:43:36-07:00","id":685812,"title":"Scions and Hunters","content":"So I know that trying to crossover Scion and Hunter is probably a difficult prospect, but I'm curious to see what the people who normally post on this board think. How do you think scions would react to the existence of humans who (might not) have godly powers that still try to fight against dark creatures lurking in the shadows? Would there be allies in the making, or is there a war on this horizon?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-02T09:22:42-07:00","id":685847,"title":"","content":"Reckoning or Vigil?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/58-lokisenna","name":"Lokisenna","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-02T09:27:16-07:00","id":685852,"title":"","content":"I think the Scions that were interested in saving humans (those with big morals, high Valor or maybe even those with Guardian) would most likely treat the Hunters much like Followers in short order.<br /> <br /> The problem with a crossover here is simply scope. A band of Hunters are supposed to find a single vampire or a single werewolf a tough fight. That would certainly be true for a low legend scion but after legend 4 the scion (I'm going with the idea that the scion would be a warrior type) would be breezing through that fight whilst the Hunters would still be finding it difficult but less deadly.<br /> <br /> After Legend 5 the scion has a minimum of 20 dots of epic stats/purviews and relics the Hunters would be dying against anything that was going to challenge the scion.<br /> <br /> Now I suppose this could work if said scion was more mental/social heavy and didn\u2019t have purviews that the antagonists were vulnerable to (hello there coven of vampire, let me introduce you to the child of Apollo our sun god in training) or the moon godling that can enchant everything we have to be silvery against therianthropes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/333-achilles","name":"Achilles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar333_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-02T09:41:59-07:00","id":685857,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lokisenna</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/685812-scions-and-hunters?p=685847#post685847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Reckoning or Vigil?</div> </div> </div> </div>Vigil.<br /> <br /> So what about the differences between the tiers? Tier 1 and 2 are probably pretty accurate for what Achilles is saying, but what about Tier 3?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-02T12:31:01-07:00","id":686053,"title":"","content":"Tier 1 (Hero) is pretty much the only tier were non-Scion characters can handle the game. At Tier 2 (Demigod), Epics start to scale crazily and are going to out pace <i>anything</i> in the World of Darkness. By Tier 3 (God)... <i>nothing</i> else competes. Gods are totally bonkers. No Hunter at all would matter even the tiniest bit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-02T13:40:30-07:00","id":686130,"title":"","content":"What Telgar said. It comes to the point that, at Demigod levels, that one Legend point (the Power trait of Scions, ala Blood Potency, Gnosis, etc), ONE, makes impossible to win against the foe with most Legend in the fight. And i'm talking about the same splat, a comparison between 3 dudes with Legend 6 and one with Legend 7. Now imagine if you have no Legend points. Absolutely insane.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Userhat Aegpts Vlrs. </span><span style=\"color:#996633\">Coren &quot;Ojos de Fuego&quot;. </span><span style=\"color:#666699\">Mithrael. </span><span style=\"color:#ffcc00\">Menehet.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1349-phersus","name":"Phersus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1349_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-02T13:59:07-07:00","id":686141,"title":"","content":"I think the Scion book mostly has this handled. A hunter group that stumbles across Scions are going to be embroiled into a religious war. Pick the hunters religion they're God is real and likely has scions. If they are going to be hunting scions the motivation is likely going to be some kind of religious war, kill the unbelievers kinda thing.<br /> <br /> I guess you can make the Hunters atheists, but that's going to rapidly meet the reality that they are simply incorrect. Zeus is right over there, he has children, they are actual divinities. It could theoretically make sense for an NPC antagonist group at low levels of scion, whatever stance you make, but for obvious reasons its not very good for a PC splat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3835-\u00falfh\u00e9\u00f0nar","name":"\u00dalfh\u00e9\u00f0nar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-02T22:16:18-07:00","id":686498,"title":"","content":"So I guess it's safe to say that even hunter's tier 3 conspiracies pretty much become a non-issue at the higher end of tier 2 scion then? Because the conspiracies have what I can only call some heavy knockout punches.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-03T06:37:43-07:00","id":686940,"title":"","content":"Tier 3 Hunter is perhaps not even a challenge at the <i>beginning</i> of demigod or even the end of Hero for a combat specc'd Scion. Your looking at someone who is is getting 8 auto successes per attack and likely has a defense at or above 15 (even against guns, surprise, basically at all times).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3835-\u00falfh\u00e9\u00f0nar","name":"\u00dalfh\u00e9\u00f0nar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-03T09:49:25-07:00","id":687195,"title":"","content":"Then I am left with a final question. What would the Aesir think of Task Force VALKYRIE?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-03T09:56:11-07:00","id":687205,"title":"","content":"All things considered they would probably be rather supportive of it as a whole. They would probably think that its an attempt to fight back at the things that attack humanity while giving the worlds most advanced and trained strike force Norse symbolism. I can't think of a reason they would dislike it unless one of them had something against the US government itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3835-\u00falfh\u00e9\u00f0nar","name":"\u00dalfh\u00e9\u00f0nar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-04T06:49:44-07:00","id":688241,"title":"","content":"A bunch of humans fighting things they are way outclassed for and dying gloriously? Sounds like einherjar fodder to me....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-04T07:57:48-07:00","id":688324,"title":"","content":"Bonus Points if Task Force VALKYRIE is actualy Run by a Valkirie as a more proactive way of recruting einherjar","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4856-alfanumerico","name":"alfanumerico","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-04T23:23:41-07:00","id":689359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Ori